From cfd11b40250ee9f1b66ad3087d34022aedce213a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <imeri@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:35:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] composefs: Put UKIs and boot entries on an XBOOTLDR partition
 next to the ESP

The Boot Loader Specification lets boot loaders read Type #1 entries and
UKIs from an Extended Boot Loader Partition (XBOOTLDR) on the ESP's disk.
That matters when the ESP is too small for UKIs, which is the usual case
next to Windows: its ESP is often 100 MB, while a UKI with a full
initramfs is 100 MB or more, and composefs keeps two or three of them.

For BLS-compatible bootloaders, look for a VFAT XBOOTLDR partition on the
ESP's disk and use it for UKIs, Type #1 entries and their binaries when
installing, upgrading and in BootedStorage. The bootloader itself, and
everything bootctl installs, stays on the ESP. GRUB setups are unchanged.
